You woke up lying on the pavement. Full moon has already showed up from behind the roof, and was shining brightly in your face. Not a single sole was around.
"Interesting, how long am I lying here? Nobody even called for medics," you thought to yourself, slowly walking along the street. At some distance you heard the sound of sirens. You turned round the corner and faced a group of people.
"Wolf! Wolf!" sounded screams. People rushed in all directions. Saving yourself from the beast you ran together with them. You looked back a couple of times, full of fright, expecting to see an open toothy mouth, but there was nobody behind. Finally you decided to separate yourself from the mad group and turned into an alleyway and hid behind a garbage can. You carefully looked from behind the cover and saw two policemen. They were walking right towards you.
"The wolf is here!" you thought to yourself, growing cold with fear.  You nervously began to look around. Suddenly you saw something dark and hairy by the opposite wall. Your heart thumped, and there was some ringing in the ears. The next moment, in spite of the panic, you made a frightening discovery: beside the opposite wall there was a mirror, that someone had thrown away. The reflection in it was yours!
"I'm a monster!" you screamed with despair. But police officers heard only a terrifying howling. It became clear that they were coming to kill you. You need to run! But where? To the left and right there were houses. Behind there was a three meter concrete fence and a bunch of armed men at the front.